# Your patch layer for this dsh profile, applied after every bundle layer:
# a top-level YAML array of loader patch entries (id-targeted config
# overrides, disables, and insert lists; `!!js` expressions allowed).
- insert:
    # Synapse vault exposed as MCP tools (local stdio child). The vault (synapse-vault)
    # and the harness stay separate — MCP is the only bridge (playbook P1).
    - id: mcp-synapse
      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client'
      config:
        serverName: synapse
        transport: stdio
        # Absolute node path: dsh scrubs the child's env, so bare `node` may not be on PATH.
        command: {{NODE}}
        args:
          - {{VAULT}}/node_modules/@eborja/synapse/bin/synapse-mcp.mjs
        cwd: {{VAULT}}
        env:
          SYNAPSE_VAULT: {{VAULT}}
          SYNAPSE_MCP_SURFACE: orchestrator
{{EXTRA_ENV}}

    # Harness-enforced Synapse loop: a claim_and_brief that is never released is caught at
    # turn-stopping and either forced back to the model or auto-released. Mechanism, not a
    # prompt instruction — the model reported success it had not achieved.
    - id: hooks-synapse
      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-hooks-claude-code'
      config:
        # Read ONCE at load — no live reload, and a bad path registers nothing silently.
        configPath: {{DSH_HOME}}/hooks/synapse-hooks.json
        projectDir: {{VAULT}}
        defaultTimeoutMs: 60000

# The order-0 persona. Presets shadow this with a scoped `deployment:persona`, but headless
# composes no preset roster, so this row IS the identity there. Keep it STATIC: order-0 sits at
# the front of the prompt, so anything varying per request would invalidate the cached prefix.
# It states the protocol; the hooks enforce it. Both, deliberately.
- id: system-prompt
  config:
    persona: >-
      You are a Synapse agent powered by the {{model}} model, working in {{cwd}}.

      The Synapse vault answers through the mcp__synapse__* tools, and reading it is always
      cheaper than guessing. Before answering a question about the vault, call synapse_brief with
      your agent id and the one hub for that domain. Before starting work that may already be
      done, call synapse_history. When the topic shifts mid-session, call synapse_recall rather
      than re-briefing.

      To delegate: call synapse_claim_and_brief with a canonical job id built from stable facts,
      hand its briefing to a subagent, and then ALWAYS close the job with synapse_spawn_release
      carrying a real summary of what the doer produced. A claim you never release blocks that job
      for its full lease and loses the result from memory; the harness will force you back to
      finish it.

      Never write db/synapse.db or any generated view, and never self-merge. Propose changes and
      stop — a human reviews them.

# Synapse briefings must arrive WHOLE. spill-policy replaces any plain-text tool result over
# maxInlineBytes with a preview + file locator; at the 50000 default a `lean` synapse_brief
# (~60KB) was silently truncated ("Omitted 10194 bytes"), forcing the agent to re-read it.
# Raised so a fat (`--profile fat`, ~120KB) brief still lands inline; genuinely runaway output
# still spills.
- id: spill-policy
  config:
    maxInlineBytes: 70000

# Let an agent pause for a human decision instead of guessing. The `user-questions` service is
# already mounted in base; only the model-facing tool is missing here (the web `standard` preset
# already carries it). One row.
- insert:
    - id: tool-ask-user
      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-ask-user'
